      "side": 1,
      "message": "See inline comment for some specific concerns.\n\nThen I\u0027m also wondering if it is correct to shutdown immediately if graceful shutdown hits an exception talking to zookeeper. Graceful shutdown of an executor is already polling for job workers to shutdown in a loop with a sleep here: https://opendev.org/zuul/zuul/src/branch/master/zuul/executor/server.py#L4305-L4307. It might be better to try to update zookeeper status each time through the loop while we continue to wait for workers to shutdown. This way graceful shutdown behaviors are preserved to the best of our ability. In theory we\u0027re going to reconnect eventually allowing the jobs to complete and report and allow us to update our component info.",
