      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this comment is accurate. exit_handler is added as the SIGINT signal handler. SIGINT is merely an interrupt that doesn\u0027t cause processes to exit. Properly handling the signal and starting a process shutdown is what causes that to happen. If we don\u0027t handle things properly because an exception is raised and get here I think we may continue to not shut down at all.\n\nA better comment might be\n\n```\nCatch and log any exceptions to make it clear why SIGINT\nhandling may not be processed as expected.\n```\n\nThen update the self.log.exception line below similarly.\n\nAdditionally the exit_handler is only called when SIGINT is sent. You can also request graceful shutdowns via the command socket\u0027s graceful command. I think any solution requires handling exceptions that may occur within the graceful shutdown routine itself.",
      "revId": "bd3a1dc9263c4515d7a5ee68b512883e08f5cb78",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
