      "side": 1,
      "message": "exit_handler is also handling SIGTERM when the command is not run as a daemon, which would be a use case when running as a container in k8s for example (see for example, executor: https://opendev.org/zuul/zuul/src/branch/master/zuul/cmd/executor.py#L118)\n\nSo maybe we should have different behaviors depending on the signal, and consider that SIGTERM means \"shut down no matter what\" ?",
